"From the very beginning I have tried with both and then, too, with the Choir to look at the diction so that the text would be well understood, so that it would be consonated," he said.
The official Czech anthem is celebrating its 175th anniversary next year.
Footage Where, My Home sounded for the first time in 1834 in the tables of the Theater of the States in Josef Kajeta-ka's original Czech Fidlova-Kroup play and arranged with the music of Franti-kroup.
She gained popularity and people made her own.
The first stump of the song after the emergence of Czechoslovakia in 1918 naturally became part of the official anthem.
