The 'tank', they call the Anglo-Speakers, but le Fabuleux Marcel de Bruxelles awakens over everyone else.
First, because of its rhyming name - although familiarly it is known as 'Marcel' - it has to do with the sport because it receives its name, according to legend, from boxer Marcel Cerdan, lover of singer Edith Piaf.
'La Marcel' stands out above the others for its excellent cotton, its unisex trim, its distinctive coat of arms and the small Belgian flag (barely recognizable) that the most iconic T-shirt models wear as detail on the neck.
And attention, because the production of the Belgian firm doesn't just focus on its tank tops.
It also includes sweatshirts, retro boxers, cashmere cardigans, cotton pants, sailor T-shirts, babies, mini shorts...
Clothes designed for underwear comfort.
