Dancer, Actress and designer, you're a very multi-pronged woman, aren't you?
I think yes, but, in the end, everything comes together and they have a lot of ties in common.
As a kid I liked the laundry; I wanted to go to my grandmother's house to dig into my aunt's wardrobes and see her clothes.
It's the bomb, it's almost better than going to the amusement park.
Then, as a dancer, I always tried to take care of how I dressed.
Already, you know the dancers very much like to do our styling for classes and rehearsals, to look at us in the mirror and feel good.
And in the acting role when they give you the wardrobe it's when you really find the character.
Then, it's all united, yes, with a lot of respect for designers and professionalism.
You didn't turn 30 long ago, did you go into crisis?
What's up?
Feeling better than ever, in my '30 I like them.
I find that the woman is made, she has experience and tastes life with fewer mistakes.
The biological cloth doesn't scare me. It doesn't scare me.
I've done the things I've loved since I was a kid and this has given me a lot of inner happiness.
Then you think of being a mom or not?
Of course, I know I'm gonna be a mum 'cause the body asks of me and, besides, I wanna be a young mom; I don't want to miss this.
As for the nominee, I don't care.
What I'm gonna do is give a lot of happiness to my son and educate him with a lot of love.
When it comes to movies, you're watching for several premieres you rotated last year.
That's right and I'm eager for them to see the light.
I, who am a woman who comes from the theater, I am very impatient and uneasy, I want everything for now and of course, it cannot be.
I'm eager for 'The Last Floor' and 'Whing to Blame the Tomb of Christ.'
Let's see that they seem...
A few days ago you debuted a catwalk with Naomi Campbell, right?
All right, well, don't say that.
I didn't get on a catwalk to modeling.
Simply, Naomi Campbell, whom I've known for a long time, to invite myself to go to London to participate in a charity parade for her 'Women for a Better World' organization and the clothes we exhibited - I took two pieces out of our collection for Mango - was auctioned to raise money for this Naomi NGO.
Guys don't know Naomi's tender heart.
They say so many things about her that, I know her, I'd tell you that so many aren't true.
Besides, I'll stick with that good part she gets involved in.
He asked me to parade for such a noble cause, but if he gets to ask me to do the pine, then too.
For benefiting third-world women, whatever it takes.
Repeated alcohol drivers will have to install the 'alcolock'
Interior wants the driver with three administrative sanctions for alcohol to have to install in his vehicle a system that prevents the drunken vehicle from ripping off, or if it does not blew.
The initiative has already been announced last June and is now already included in the annual report of the Attorney General's Office, according to which it is a pilot project that will last for one year.
Its purpose is the reinsertion of the driver, so he will also receive a road re-education course.
In addition to the Attorney General &apos; s Office for Road Safety, the Directorate-General for Trafficking (DGT) and the Technological Institute for Automobile Safety Foundation (FITSA) will participate.
According to the statistics, between 30% and 75 per cent of self-driving motorists more than once for drunk driving catch the car again.
Alcolock would avoid it because it is a system connected to the vehicle that measures the spiral alcohol rate and prevents it from booting the automobile if the driver does not blew abtes; or when a concentration of alcohol is detected it is higher than that allowed.
Its cost is more than 1,000 euros and would be borne by the sanctioned.
In this sense, a study carried out in the United States in 2007 showed that vehicles equipped with these devices reduce by up to 65% violations during the first year of implantation.
And in Spain it is estimated that it could save the lives of 115 people each year.
The measure adheres to administrative sanctions for two reasons: to address such conduct before they result in criminal offences.
And to facilitate its implementation, since the legal reform can be carried out on an ordinary basis, and, however, the necessary reform through the criminal procedure requires a reform of an organic law.
The device has not yet been available on the Spanish market in any commercial modality, although it has already been experimentally implanted in some commercial and public service vehicles.
Precisely tomorrow the Congress of Deputies will vote tomorrow on an initiative of the PSOE proposing to install this system on school buses, just as it has been carried out in France.
In Mexico and without 'peep-toes'
