Embraer maintains its delivery forecasts for 2008
The Brazilian aeronautics company has 215 planes delivered this year despite threats of recession that weigh on the global economy.
The world's fourth aeronautical builder, Embraer, maintains its delivery forecasts for 2008 with 215 devices delivered, Embraer President Fredrico Fleury Curado reaffirmed.
