The New York Stock Exchange blamed a historic fall last Monday after the House of Representatives rejected the Paulson plan to save the banks: the Dow Jones lost 6.98 per cent, a never-before-season loss of almost 800 points, and the Nasdaq by 9.14 per cent.
The Dow Jones industrial index fell 777.68 to 10,365.45 points.
