"Either it passes announcing the fall of a financial institution in the U.S. in the U.S.," Ms Piegza stressed.
After the bankruptcy of Washington Mutual last Friday, the authorities organized the purchase of Wachovia's banking activities by their rival Citigroup.
In Europe, the crisis accelerated drastically, leading to emergency interventions for the benefit of banks in the United Kingdom, Benelux, Iceland and Germany, which shows that the markets face "not only a crisis in the United States but a global crisis ," FTN Financial added.
The obligating market rose dramatically.
Ten-year treasury bond yield retreated by 3,632 per cent, against 3,827 per cent on Friday afternoon, and the 30-year bond by 4,161 per cent, against 4,357 per cent the previous day.
