Québec's Democratic Action seemed to support the adoption of a North Plan by the government.
"But what's desired, is that this isn't just a spectacle ," said leader Sebastien Proulx, replacing Mario Dumont, who returns on vacation today.
Letters - A Disgraced Country
It is Mr. Vic Toews, former Minister of "Jusstice" in the Harper cabinet, which was allowed last summer to say that Luisa Arbour was a "shame" for Canada.
Disgracing thus this woman who led an incessant fight for justice and who deserves all of our admiration that says everything about the relations of the Prime Minister and Stephen Harper.
