Mp3 readers under accusation, put hearing at risk
Listening high-volume music for a long period of time using portable musical gadgets like Mp3 readers can cause permanent hearing injuries.
The European Commission, which in a statement published in Bruxel cites the opinion of the Scientific Committee on Emerging and recently identified Health Risk (Csrseri) of the U, published today.
"From this scientific opinion it is read in the note - it emerges that 5-10% of those who, for a period of at least 5 years, listen to music with portable musical devices weekly for more than an hour a day having the apparatus at high volume risk a permanent loss of the auditory capacity."
