Open Office, echo the 3rd "anti-Microsoft" package.
It's the launch day of the OpenOffice.org 3.0, the open source personal productivity suite that aims to always attract more users, from the house to the office to public service professionals, as a free alternative to the well-known Microsoft Office.
After a work of almost a year by volunteer developers, of which their backs are monitored by SUN Microsystem, the new Open Office is shown to the public with several novelties: to the welcome screen and less ruthless magazine interface, more consistent ones are added, such as compatibility for the Apple Mac OS X operating system and the support for the new ODF format(Open Document Format) 1.2, the latest ISO standard version.
Attention also put to multi-function with the 2007 Office suite, Open Office is able to open the documents with Microsoft's new extension (.docx, .xlsx, .pptx).
Interesting some specific functions of some modules such as the one that allows to reduce the dimension of the PowerPoint presentation, useful for example, to send it via an electronic post, or the possibility of importing the PDF file in the graphic elaboration module, conserving the original aspect of the page.
Always on this front you can create "hybrid PDF documents," which accumulate graph typical of Adobe's format with the elements of a spreadsheet or a text processor.
Collaboration is an element that has received different improvements within the applications: in the spreadsheet they can intervene in various users, avoiding the conflicts of the modities, in the elaboration of texts to each collaborator is given a color in the comment for a better recognition in the review phase.
Some companies are also working to bring some OpenOffice functions to the Web (on the cloud, over the clouds), and in the coming weeks they should deliver the final result.
The Italian version can be downloaded at http://it.openoffice.org/download/3.0.0/download300.html and was added to the groin who has been in the Mirror since Friday.
In addition, for Windows and Mac OS, as the suite normally is also available for the Linux operating system.
Upon request you can also send the installation cd at home or to work.
And if the topic of free can be a hook for the dissemination in the houses, it is in business area that Open Office the suite tests, it tries the big bet, being able to already have several projects carried out in the public administration and in the schools.
And there's not even a shortage of the realities offered by an ideal training, consultation and assistance service for small and medium-sized enterprises, in which businesses could be opened.
Open Office is composed of five main modules: Writer, for video writing the corresponding Word; Calc, is the spreadsheet that replaces Excel; Impress, for the presentation of Powerpoint; Dbase, eating in the case of the well-known Access is the program that consents to work on the base data; and finally Draw the graphic module.
Objective for 2008 is to reach 5 million download, and considering that until today we have reached almost 3 million 600 thousand, with the departure of the new version it is likely that the expected figure can be exceeded.
